{"title":"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3=\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3=</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2eb65a95e4740345dd6809403aff78cbde25309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\pi/2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130591afb17e8bdcc9d7334e4fcc26d57a8f65bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2[\\cos(a)\\sin(a) + \\cos(4a)\\sin(2a) + \\cos(9a)\\sin(3a) + \\cdots + \\cos(n^2a)\\sin(na)]\\]\" width=\"548\" height=\"20\" />\nis an integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Trigonometric identity\">product-to-sum identities</a>, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae61889cb3f7cfaa77c4e0fcbbe49089e3d95ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos a \\sin b = \\sin (a+b) - \\sin (a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, this reduces to a telescope series: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417655839b4578551543e9697b058fe3d9c42e97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{k=1}^{n} 2\\cos(k^2a)\\sin(ka) &amp;= \\sum_{k=1}^{n} [\\sin(k(k+1)a) - \\sin((k-1)ka)]\\\\ &amp;= -\\sin(0) + \\sin(2a)- \\sin(2a) + \\sin(6a) - \\cdots - \\sin((n-1)na) + \\sin(n(n+1)a)\\\\ &amp;= -\\sin(0) + \\sin(n(n+1)a) = \\sin(n(n+1)a) \\end{align*}\" width=\"797\" height=\"99\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6bf14a46025fc51ea354846e2eb3d5f45ba5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\left(\\frac{n(n+1)\\pi}{2008}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" /> to be an integer; this can be only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f0478d311225334208821f5e81b92d5e163654a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{-1,0,1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, which occur when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79b94c03dd8fa85c54047875c314da936a0fc48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{n(n+1)}{2008}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"40\" /> is an integer. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/2191036b11ac2758a88bfa900c3a9459719abf6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1004 = 2^2 \\cdot 251 | n(n+1) \\Longrightarrow 251 | n, n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"321\" height=\"19\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> isn't divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so 1004 doesn't divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/2356f6df2d01ecd0df4268e023f1dbd1999d3f1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1) = 250 \\cdot 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef2adb48b4a3aa9ae3157fff37c19db08d94f9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{251}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" /> is the smallest such integer.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We proceed with complex trigonometry. We know that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/2992e40eb06a3ae3b5404fa1267032425d36442f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( z + \\dfrac{1}{z} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"144\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a09e2d947471bc626c6fd65277498fa57848590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{2i} \\left( z - \\dfrac{1}{z} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"148\" height=\"43\" /> for some complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> on the unit circle. Similarly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b301361403b9d717d0101676532068a72dc9cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos n \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( z^n + \\dfrac{1}{z^n} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"173\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e008bfc326cae6919d4c10a64bd81ca39544200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin n \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{2i} \\left(z^n - \\dfrac{1}{z^n} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"177\" height=\"43\" />. Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd295b624ea5cd3b169e44184f2da0e54614709e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos n^2 a \\sin n a = \\dfrac{1}{4i} \\left( z^{n^2} + \\dfrac{1}{z^{n^2}} \\right) \\left( z^{n} - \\dfrac{1}{z^n} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"341\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b86469c904a8eb8f804d221373553594ef671c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\dfrac{1}{4i} \\left( z^{n^2 + n} - \\dfrac{1}{z^{n^2 + n}} - z^{n^2 - n} + \\dfrac{1}{z^{n^2 - n}} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"312\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7607500367455d938893bf06255c8a0d17a6dbe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2i} \\left(z^{n^2 + n} - \\dfrac{1}{z^{n^2 + n}} \\right) - \\dfrac{1}{2i} \\left(z^{n^2 - n} - \\dfrac{1}{z^{n^2 - n}} \\right) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"402\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51fa634d69f3a93e725869cd21dfc4fe0953c232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( \\sin ((n^2 + n)a) - \\sin ((n^2 - n)a) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"294\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea3fd87f46982ef9ae2af39a2d0570664f4be38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( \\sin(((n+1)^2 - (n+1))a) - \\sin((n^2 - n)a) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"385\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>which clearly telescopes! Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> outside the brackets cancels with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4a7df1100efe353cc612d5d1c289c22d5bf8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> inside, we see that the sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426b2ee32f251eda36f2c568379ab22a1fe647a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin ((2^2 - 2)a) - \\sin ((1^2 - 1)a) + \\sin ((3^3 - 3)a) - \\sin ((2^2 - 2)a) \\cdots + \\sin (((n+1)^2 - (n+1))a) - \\sin ((n^2 - n)a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"880\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc97ba32e121b6ff6e565e62d9eb653f9620062f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\sin (((n+1)^2 - (n+1))a) - \\sin(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fece0ff305eb1ae5448639ca5961466ecfd3f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\sin ((n^2 + n)a) - 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/2539c7badea59f444289284f80fa63366cb93b9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{n(n+1) \\pi}{2008} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"149\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>This expression takes on an integer value iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e29e359441ee702cecf272958c2cfdb77720c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2n(n+1)}{2008} = \\dfrac{n(n+1)}{1004}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"39\" /> is an integer; that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a582c93fe8eaaf77f06162a2f954d93b1be2568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1004 \\mid n(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3ec98227f7c8f15968d21962862e01329ecbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1004 = 2^2 \\cdot 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b74a848a7297adf02df85df7f6c37b94692abf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$251 \\mid n(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. Since we want the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we see that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57468b268ba9e4794b081f52e673b22e6f54935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n,n+1} = 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd24a29e72cb6498a6f5987d0e7eb003548e2504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1 = 251 \\rightarrow n=250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"183\" height=\"14\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/292752c77039e71f2e969954dea47e1d44118949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1) = 250(251)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />, which is clearly not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99b4773ff3d3ef9cc970d28784430be58c24185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd0f67cde921ba951e0d1906018d9a73d28a2d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a582c93fe8eaaf77f06162a2f954d93b1be2568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1004 \\mid n(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b73d920fb16466a208ef1beeb3c0481a69d463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{251}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>It should be noted that the product-to-sum rules follow directly from complex trigonometry, so this solution is essentially equivalent to the solution above.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h1><span id=\"Solution_3.3D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3=\">Solution 3=</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3=\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fab11d11bb858950adf4769a9b0f2693a5a11d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{i\\theta}=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac65c011afd85c340d4ac56f11000fdd5315d20c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\cos(\\theta )+i\\sin(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f970a95fe7901b93e620b2ee3a9f586cffc722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{z}=\\cos(\\theta)-i\\sin(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"164\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We solve this system to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c1e86cb05d378d915a10f1b0b7aa133950e32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos(\\theta)=\\frac{z+z^{-1}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322d70eb80547f911657d9b7905f10985f61e26b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(\\theta)=\\frac{z-z^{-1}}{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>We see that each term in the sequence is in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a866ec5250f5126c2a0cca98d4d944c4f057a9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2cos(k^(2)*a)(ka)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656b863d35e824e7fe2f78a5941c950779bd8998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(k^2 a)=\\frac{e^{ik^2a} + e^{-ik^2a}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"198\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/834512d79672686ba417f8f4c82cc4d8340396eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(ka)=\\frac{e^{ika} - e^{-ika}}{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>When we plug these values into our expression, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/90850b4662ace50bc36897b248d4df7ae2bf81cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos(k^2 a)\\sin(ka)=\\frac{1}{2i} *(e^{i(k^2+k)a} + e^{-i(-k^2+k)a} -e^{i(k^2-k)a} - e^{i(-k^2-k)a})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"563\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We write out the first couple terms of our sequence and find that the whole sequence telescopes until the last term. We write out our last term as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b99167309fef761112583f54dee5b13fe8e0f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{e^{i(n^2 + n)a} - e^{i(-n^2 -n)a}}{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" />, which we can convert back to trigonometry.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb6138e08d4f3750b26277603022f3b680adcd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cos(n^2 +n)a + i\\sin(n^2 +n)a - \\cos(-n^2 -n)a - i\\sin(-n^2 - n)a}{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"514\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751b6658dd43d56d98a544fb9447eb92df37ee91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin((n^2 + n)a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081bf0417da2140657aad909a14ca6c3ff8b77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> to be an integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>We can write an equation to solve now by substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd4b93ea2c9a2864b3f8f56b65cd212e36bece1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(n^2 + n)\\pi}{2008}=\\frac{k\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>We cross-multiply to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59c152fa6d3f728cf51aca4b60da3178eddc3819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1)=1004k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> has a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f1c4193e8c21c6384954b4b13d24d9ddcf0933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$251$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and the other one is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We see that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3b6295a359c2f2fbfb9598ee1e409c481dbb59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> will be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f550e0dc9e9f31358cf34380dee446d759498a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\boxed{251}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Similar problem for more practice:</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 12</a> uses the other product-to-sum relation and is slightly more involved. \n</p><p>-unhappyfarmer\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II\" title=\"2008 AIME II\">2008 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017214515\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 440/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14461/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,te